WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.467
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.501
Thank you for watching at home.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.100
Happy Cinco de Mayo!

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.234
Yeah, it's that one day when
people are excited to hear

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:21.434
someone say, "I've got Corona!"

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:25.734
But what a day.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.334
After two years of
working from home,

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.734
it was nice to have those
vaguely problematic parties

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.000
back in the office again.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.267
Yeah.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:33.734
That's right --
it's Cinco de Mayo,

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.601
and I guess that explains this
announcement that I saw today.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:39.968
-Cinco de Mayo is a special day
in Mexico's history,

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.868
but, sadly, not many people know

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.601
what this holiday commemorates.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.501
-And neither do we!
[ Air horn blows ]

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:48.667
So come on down to Chili's for
a classic margarita

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:52.601
that we've turned neon blue so
you can get conquistador-crunk.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.367
Chili's -- arrivederci!

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.901
[ Air horn blows ]

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.801
-What?

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.434
It sounds like
a great deal at Chili's.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.367
And this is fun.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.167
7-Eleven celebrated by offering

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:09.734
three spicy breakfast empanadas
and a coffee for just $4.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:10.968
Yeah, it's great.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.868
You just walk in and order the
"El Baño."

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:16.133
They know what to do.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.334
-Oy!
-Listen to this.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.167
I read that each year on
Cinco de Mayo,

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:22.801
Americans eat about
80 million pounds of avocados.

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.367
Wow! 80 million pounds.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.434
-Oh, man.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.133
I love the food on
Cinco de Mayo.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.501
-Cool. That's nice, Tariq.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.434
-Hey, you want to know what my
favorite Cinco de Mayo food is?

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.701
-Uh, I mean, not right now,

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:40.601
but we can definitely talk later
if you want to

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:41.667
talk about which foods --

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.200
-Tacos!

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.501
♪♪

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.534
If you're looking for
a spicy meal to give you

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:53.934
all the feels,
then you've got to try some

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.667
food from this dude.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:00.801
I'm talking about
Tariq's Tacos Fantasticos!

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.734
They'll make your mouth go loco

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:05.434
while you sip some
rum and Diet Coke-o.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:10.801
All you need to make
these zesty-ass tacos are

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:17.067
tortillas...chicken...cheese...

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:22.267
peppers...diced onions...guac...

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.834
and a little bit of cilantro.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:27.033
Ladies --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:33.567
Hey, ladies,
these tacos are DTF.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:39.200
By which I mean, delicious,
Tariq-approved, and fabuloso.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.901
And if you're feeling like
it's naughty o'clock,

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:45.868
then do yourself a favor
and squeeze some lime.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.534
-Oh, wow.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.734
-God damn!

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:57.701
Every taste is like
a gift for your face.

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.534
Back to you, Jimmy.
-Wow.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.234
Oh, my gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:03.501
Wow.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.367
Tariq, those look great.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.400
Those look great.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.734
-Yeah, I don't need
your approval

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:11.033
to feel good about
myself, homey.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:13.534
Get back to your show.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.167
-Alright, meanwhile, today...

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:29.100
Who's that character, man?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.634
-He cracked himself up.
Who was that guy?

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:33.367
-Great, dude.

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.567
Meanwhile, today,
President Biden hosted

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.868
a Cinco de Mayo reception
in the Rose Garden

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.801
with the First Lady of Mexico,
yeah.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.734
Biden talked about
the warm relationship

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.601
between the U.S. and Mexico.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.567
It's better than Trump's
message on Cinco de Mayo,

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:51.334
which was,
"Think outside the bun."

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.901
Speaking of Biden, apparently,
he's been telling allies

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:57.534
that he's almost certainly going
to run in 2024 if Trump does.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.067
Yep, Biden against Trump.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:00.300
It's great news
for all the people

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.834
who wish it was 2020 again.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.334
Right now, all the debate
moderators are like, "Not it!"

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.567
Yeah.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:07.834
Some business news.

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:10.434
Airbnb just announced
that it will be enforcing

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:13.367
strict anti-party measures
on summer holidays,

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.667
like Memorial Day
and Fourth of July.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.067
Yep, it's serious.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.400
If you break the partying rules,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.701
a person you've never met before
will be furious at you.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.567
Hey, I saw that Mountain Dew

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.701
just released a new drink
called Purple Thunder.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.767
Here it is. Look at this.
Ooh, yeah.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:30.968
-Ooh!

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.000
-Looks like someone put
Barney the Dinosaur

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.734
through a Nutribullet.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:37.400
There are only
two ingredients --

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.501
caffeine and Robitussin.

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:41.534
Can we see that again?

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.167
And the bottle
was perfectly straight

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.667
until they poured in
the Mountain Dew.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:45.701
It's interesting.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.167
Did you guys see this?

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.834
Yesterday, the Houston Astros
took on the Seattle Mariners,

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:53.033
and one of the Astros players,
José Altuve, had a rough at bat.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.133
Take a look at this.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.467
-Oh, my!

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.868
-Oh!

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.300
-Give him all the time.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.834
-Yeah.
-Whoa!

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.133
-"Give him all the time."

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.534
Yeah. Ooh.

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:10.501
Two balls, one strike.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.367
I know. That's...
[ Rimshot ]

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.133
-Oy!

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:16.501
-Right after that, he ordered
an ice cream in a tiny helmet

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:17.701
and shoved it down his pants.

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.567
I heard about a family
in Massachusetts

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.033
who thought that
they rescued a lost puppy,

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:26.901
but it actually turned
out to be a baby coyote.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.901
They knew it was
a coyote when it tried to

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.801
blow up the house with
dynamite and run off a cliff.

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:35.200
Did you guys hear about this?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.133
Today, after a United flight
landed in Chicago,

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.801
a man opened the emergency exit,
walked out on the wing,

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:42.334
and slid down to the tarmac.

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:44.868
Anyway, happy Cinco de Mayo,
everyone.

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:47.467
Be safe out there, you know?

